1
00:00:00,352 --> 00:00:05,359
Warden — an SRE agent for long-running compute jobs

2
00:00:05,359 --> 00:00:10,862
A live machine is not correct training. Finished is not intact.

3
00:00:10,862 --> 00:00:19,804
Right now: one job training on a Spot machine in Compute Engine

4
00:00:19,804 --> 00:00:31,058
Warden is watching it — heartbeats, phase markers, signed completion markers

5
00:00:31,058 --> 00:01:34,817
The job is about to hit a GPU out-of-memory error at step 600

6
00:01:34,817 --> 00:01:48,027
It died. Warden opened an incident in seconds — nobody was watching

7
00:01:48,027 --> 00:01:57,795
Evidence first: the log line, quoted from the run's own log

8
00:01:57,795 --> 00:02:38,004
Then the diagnosis — and every quote is checked against the raw log before anything happens

9
00:02:38,004 --> 00:02:56,621
Warden decided by itself: resume at half the batch size. No human was asked.

10
00:02:56,621 --> 00:04:22,888
And then it checks the world: did the new run actually pass the step it died at?

11
00:04:22,888 --> 00:04:33,099
Some actions Warden may not take alone. Those go to a phone.

12
00:04:33,099 --> 00:11:40,790
A card is waiting in Discord right now — the operator approves it from there

13
00:11:40,790 --> 00:11:50,451
Every approval carries its blast radius, its cost, and an expiry

14
00:11:50,451 --> 00:12:04,319
Every intent and every result is written down, whoever asked for it

15
00:12:04,319 --> 00:12:19,554
Warden never deletes anything — that is denied by IAM, not by good intentions

16
00:12:19,554 --> 00:12:29,428
And one button stops all of it

17
00:12:29,428 --> 00:12:39,095
Frozen. Warden observes and proposes, but acts on nothing.

18
00:12:39,095 --> 00:12:46,131
A live machine is not correct training. Finished is not intact. Warden watches the work.

19
00:12:46,131 --> 00:12:47,358

